1
00:00:19,553 --> 00:00:21,088
Are those my things?

2
00:00:21,103 --> 00:00:22,871
What are you going to do?

3
00:00:23,508 --> 00:00:25,931
I'm replacing all your old clothes
with new ones.

4
00:00:25,931 --> 00:00:27,391
Outfits that suit you better.

5
00:00:27,391 --> 00:00:30,499
And as for this,

6
00:00:30,499 --> 00:00:34,298
let's change this to a newer model
with a more secure connection.

7
00:00:34,298 --> 00:00:36,834
Baste, you take care of that.

8
00:00:36,834 --> 00:00:38,357
How is she?

9
00:00:38,357 --> 00:00:40,425
We haven't talked to each other.

10
00:00:40,425 --> 00:00:42,366
Why, did you fight?

11
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:43,666
No, we didn't.

12
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:46,475
I tried to call her
but she cannot be reached.

13
00:00:46,475 --> 00:00:49,968
I don't think it's a matter
of WiFi or signal.

14
00:00:49,968 --> 00:00:54,545
Knowing Rogelio,
they took away Florence's cell phone.

15
00:00:54,545 --> 00:00:56,397
Why would they do that, Grandpa?

16
00:00:56,397 --> 00:01:01,384
You must understand, Nero,
that the Almeros are a very proud family.

17
00:01:01,384 --> 00:01:04,196
They are one of the oldest families.

18
00:01:04,196 --> 00:01:08,059
And they are very sensitive
with their reputation.

19
00:01:08,059 --> 00:01:11,089
And now that Florence is with them,

20
00:01:11,089 --> 00:01:15,360
I'm sure she's going to be changed
and become an Almero.

21
00:01:40,158 --> 00:01:41,466
Florence, can we talk?

22
00:01:41,466 --> 00:01:45,671
Can we talk later?
I'll find a way to talk to you.

23
00:01:45,671 --> 00:01:48,121
We're your friends, Florence.
We're not a threat.

24
00:01:48,121 --> 00:01:50,318
- Are you okay?
- Hey Mister, don't push!

25
00:01:50,318 --> 00:01:52,177
- Hey, that's enough!
- Don't push us!

26
00:01:52,177 --> 00:01:54,105
Mister, they're not my enemies!

27
00:01:54,105 --> 00:01:55,206
- Don't do that.
- Hey, stop!

28
00:01:55,206 --> 00:01:56,660
- I said don't push us.
- Mister, stop it.

29
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:59,504
They are not enemies! They are my friends!

30
00:02:49,014 --> 00:02:52,117
My child, this is Mother.

31
00:02:52,117 --> 00:02:53,985
And Father, too.

32
00:02:55,687 --> 00:02:59,436
Mother, Father...

33
00:02:59,436 --> 00:03:02,928
Florence, we miss you so much.

34
00:03:02,928 --> 00:03:05,831
Your father and I are always praying for you.

35
00:03:05,831 --> 00:03:08,400
We also hear Mass and say a novena.

36
00:03:10,461 --> 00:03:13,598
<i>I heard your conversation earlier.</i>

37
00:03:14,232 --> 00:03:16,835
It's good that you're able
to eat properly there.

38
00:03:18,143 --> 00:03:21,233
Do you want us to send you rambutan?

39
00:03:21,233 --> 00:03:25,139
No need, Father.
I might burn down the whole mansion.

40
00:03:25,139 --> 00:03:28,594
Don't be shocked that
we're here in the mansion.

41
00:03:28,594 --> 00:03:33,178
Yes, Florence,
Grandpa Garp hired us to cook for them.

42
00:03:33,178 --> 00:03:35,214
That's good.

43
00:03:35,214 --> 00:03:42,166
Tristan asked me to make a mango pie
with Guimaras Mangoes.

44
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:46,058
And Troy wanted a Paella Valencia,

45
00:03:46,058 --> 00:03:47,996
a Ventura, and Negra too.

46
00:03:47,996 --> 00:03:50,195
<i>So I hit him with the Paella pan.</i>

47
00:03:50,195 --> 00:03:53,332
And I suddenly made sushi.

48
00:03:53,332 --> 00:03:56,034
Aldus was dreaming about sushi,

49
00:03:56,034 --> 00:03:59,839
<i>and I felt like I was having a nightmare.</i>

50
00:03:59,839 --> 00:04:03,513
Owen is my favorite because he likes eggs.

51
00:04:03,513 --> 00:04:06,917
I told him to eat hot dogs too.

52
00:04:08,046 --> 00:04:11,350
Oh, Mother, Father,
they're just pranking you.

53
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:13,324
Just have a little more patience.

54
00:04:13,324 --> 00:04:16,363
Don't worry about us, Florence.

55
00:04:16,363 --> 00:04:19,794
We can handle these brothers.

56
00:04:19,794 --> 00:04:23,911
And Florence,
the Ferell Brothers is a misnomer,

57
00:04:23,911 --> 00:04:26,265
because the truth is, they're all cousins.

58
00:04:26,265 --> 00:04:28,200
It should be Ferell Cousins.

59
00:04:31,326 --> 00:04:33,305
Yes, that's right.

60
00:04:33,305 --> 00:04:36,563
Those brothers are a misnomer.

61
00:04:36,563 --> 00:04:39,299
Do you already know their WiFi password?

62
00:04:46,057 --> 00:04:48,160
Thank you, Nero.

63
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,649
Thank you for doing this.

64
00:04:50,649 --> 00:04:53,025
Did you come up with this idea?

65
00:04:53,025 --> 00:04:57,368
I don't want to take all the credit,
but yes.

66
00:04:57,368 --> 00:04:58,870
Everything was my idea.

67
00:04:58,870 --> 00:05:02,491
So yes, I'm taking all the credit.

68
00:05:02,491 --> 00:05:06,804
I thought you'll try to be humble,
but you're still arrogant.

69
00:05:11,445 --> 00:05:13,007
I miss you.

70
00:05:13,838 --> 00:05:16,288
I miss you so much.

71
00:05:16,288 --> 00:05:18,190
Really?

72
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,827
Maybe you're just saying that.

73
00:05:20,827 --> 00:05:22,562
It's true.

74
00:05:23,507 --> 00:05:26,162
If it's true...

75
00:05:26,162 --> 00:05:29,108
What in particular do you miss about me?

76
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:32,460
A lot.

77
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:35,001
What in particular?

78
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,509
Too many to mention.

79
00:05:37,509 --> 00:05:42,280
You're annoying.
If you don't answer me, I'll beat you.

80
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,624
Well, that's one of them.

81
00:05:44,624 --> 00:05:46,818
I miss your snarl...

82
00:05:46,818 --> 00:05:48,508
Your snarl of love.

83
00:05:48,508 --> 00:05:50,562
I don't know about you.

84
00:05:52,257 --> 00:05:53,658
<i>That's another one.</i>

85
00:05:53,658 --> 00:05:56,461
You being dismissive when you're thrilled.

86
00:05:58,515 --> 00:06:01,775
Am I very predictable?

87
00:06:01,775 --> 00:06:03,535
Never.

88
00:06:03,535 --> 00:06:07,639
Every day you surprise me,
just like right now.

89
00:06:07,639 --> 00:06:08,234
You surprised me

90
00:06:08,234 --> 00:06:11,710
that you were able
to handle this big change in your life.

91
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:14,048
<i>I am admiring you more and more.</i>

92
00:06:14,048 --> 00:06:17,282
<i>And I love you so much more.</i>

93
00:06:29,946 --> 00:06:31,778
Celestina?

94
00:06:32,764 --> 00:06:34,628
Yes?

95
00:06:34,628 --> 00:06:36,441
Are you okay?

96
00:06:38,457 --> 00:06:41,853
Thank you, Grandpa Garp,
for helping me and Lydia.

97
00:06:41,853 --> 00:06:45,724
We will consider this
a huge debt of gratitude.

98
00:06:45,724 --> 00:06:51,930
I told you that Florence is
already a member of this family.

99
00:06:51,930 --> 00:06:54,939
And even if she changes her surname,

100
00:06:54,939 --> 00:06:58,503
she will remain a member of this household.

101
00:07:00,072 --> 00:07:02,876
Excuse me, Don Ferell.

102
00:07:03,970 --> 00:07:10,345
Has someone seen the real killer
of Florence's real mother?

103
00:07:11,552 --> 00:07:15,987
As a matter of fact, no one has yet.

104
00:07:15,987 --> 00:07:18,403
According to my research,

105
00:07:18,403 --> 00:07:25,065
the death of Alyanna Almero remains unsolved.

106
00:07:25,065 --> 00:07:27,793
Unsolved or unresolved?

107
00:07:27,793 --> 00:07:29,276
Dissolved.

108
00:07:30,877 --> 00:07:32,737
That's what I'm afraid of.

109
00:07:32,737 --> 00:07:35,831
There's still a threat to Florence's life,

110
00:07:35,831 --> 00:07:39,527
because there's still a danger
with the Almeros.

111
00:07:39,527 --> 00:07:47,791
Wait, do you remember anything that night
when you found Florence?

112
00:07:49,394 --> 00:07:51,331
Do I still remember anything?

113
00:07:52,249 --> 00:07:54,807
<i>Careful.</i>

114
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:55,774
What's with you?

115
00:07:55,774 --> 00:07:58,597
Maybe you need a wheelchair.
Do you need a wheelchair?

116
00:07:58,597 --> 00:08:00,875
My tummy hurts. I feel so heavy.

117
00:08:00,875 --> 00:08:04,336
Why wouldn't your tummy hurt
when you sucked all the brain?

118
00:08:04,336 --> 00:08:07,551
What's with you?
You know me, I'm fond of brainy.

119
00:08:07,551 --> 00:08:09,621
- Brainy?
- Especially when it comes to the beef broth.

120
00:08:09,621 --> 00:08:12,300
Don't complain because
you ate a lot too, okay?

121
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:16,661
Well, I didn't eat.

122
00:08:16,661 --> 00:08:18,063
What do you mean you didn't eat?

123
00:08:18,063 --> 00:08:23,369
I ordered three cups of rice,
but you took another one.

124
00:08:23,369 --> 00:08:25,957
Wait, I feel dizzy.

125
00:08:25,957 --> 00:08:28,693
Oh no, that's what I'm telling you.

126
00:08:28,693 --> 00:08:31,096
Okay later, let's drink medicine.

127
00:08:31,955 --> 00:08:33,244
What medicine?

128
00:08:33,244 --> 00:08:35,867
Well, I'll take care of it.

129
00:08:35,867 --> 00:08:39,285
Let's go, you're sleepy, and your head hurts.

130
00:08:39,285 --> 00:08:40,405
Let's go home.

131
00:08:40,405 --> 00:08:41,808
- Let's go.
- I feel dizzy.

132
00:08:41,808 --> 00:08:43,338
Okay.

133
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:49,915
Mister, have you seen a woman pass by here?

134
00:08:51,049 --> 00:08:52,619
No.

135
00:08:53,518 --> 00:08:54,853
No?

136
00:08:54,853 --> 00:08:56,385
No.

137
00:08:57,689 --> 00:09:00,572
Okay, thank you.

138
00:09:01,726 --> 00:09:04,765
What was that? He suddenly...

139
00:09:04,765 --> 00:09:07,158
Addicts nowadays...

140
00:09:08,830 --> 00:09:11,469
Do you remember what this guy looked like?

141
00:09:11,469 --> 00:09:13,666
Did you recognize his face?

142
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:18,775
Are you okay?

143
00:09:19,432 --> 00:09:21,079
Yes, I'm having allergies.

144
00:09:21,079 --> 00:09:25,893
Maybe I'm not used to staying in
a very clean room.

145
00:09:28,926 --> 00:09:35,182
Look, I don't blame you
if you don't want to see or talk to me.

146
00:09:35,791 --> 00:09:40,909
I just came here to say... I'm sorry.

147
00:09:46,971 --> 00:09:49,910
I know I might have been
too harsh with you earlier,

148
00:09:49,910 --> 00:09:52,909
but I hope you can understand
where I'm coming from.

149
00:09:54,312 --> 00:09:58,987
I lost you once, Celestina,
and it broke my heart.

150
00:10:00,799 --> 00:10:06,519
Now that I have you,
I will do everything to protect you.

151
00:10:06,519 --> 00:10:10,949
But the Ferell brothers
have become my friends.

152
00:10:10,949 --> 00:10:15,834
And I've become close to Grandpa Garp
because I spent a long time with him.

153
00:10:15,834 --> 00:10:18,876
We're like one family.

154
00:10:18,876 --> 00:10:22,789
Do I really need to avoid them?

155
00:10:25,513 --> 00:10:27,719
I'll show you something.

156
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:38,232
I can't remember.

157
00:10:41,263 --> 00:10:43,232
Just relax.

158
00:10:43,232 --> 00:10:46,825
Don't be pressured.
You'll eventually remember.

159
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:54,442
Federico, maybe we should
shake your brain a bit

160
00:10:54,442 --> 00:10:58,131
so you can remember the details.

161
00:10:58,131 --> 00:11:00,078
You know, buddy, that's effective.

162
00:11:00,078 --> 00:11:02,426
Even if you hit your head with a stone.

163
00:11:03,036 --> 00:11:06,317
Stop it, both of you.
You're full of nonsense.

164
00:11:06,317 --> 00:11:09,450
What if I hit your brains?

165
00:11:09,450 --> 00:11:12,924
Babycakes, just relax.

166
00:11:12,924 --> 00:11:15,126
We need to lighten the mood.

167
00:11:15,126 --> 00:11:21,309
I don't want Federico to get stressed,
because he has a heart ailment.

168
00:11:23,268 --> 00:11:25,561
Don't get pressured, Federico.

169
00:11:25,561 --> 00:11:28,223
Take as much time as you want.

170
00:11:29,161 --> 00:11:34,612
But no matter how small the detail
you remember...

171
00:11:36,361 --> 00:11:37,973
Give it to us.

172
00:11:37,973 --> 00:11:42,223
Maybe that can help us protect Florence.

173
00:11:48,953 --> 00:11:51,841
She was the love of my life.

174
00:11:51,841 --> 00:11:54,051
You should've known her.

175
00:11:55,413 --> 00:11:59,692
It's unfortunate
that we spent so much time with her,

176
00:11:59,692 --> 00:12:03,614
while you weren't able to know her.

177
00:12:05,758 --> 00:12:10,989
Actually, I always dream about her.

178
00:12:22,903 --> 00:12:25,129
Ouch.

179
00:12:25,129 --> 00:12:26,764
Really?

180
00:12:26,764 --> 00:12:32,296
Yes, I always see her face in my dreams

181
00:12:32,296 --> 00:12:40,029
but I don't know if it was just a dream
or a memory that she left in me.

182
00:12:41,446 --> 00:12:43,271
Maybe it's both.

183
00:12:44,670 --> 00:12:46,784
She left the memories to show you

184
00:12:46,784 --> 00:12:50,041
how much she protected you
with all her heart.

185
00:12:50,041 --> 00:12:53,714
And the dreams are her way of saying

186
00:12:53,714 --> 00:12:56,994
to be careful with our family's enemies.

187
00:13:00,869 --> 00:13:04,736
She was killed by the Ferells, Celestina.

188
00:13:04,736 --> 00:13:07,912
They killed your mother.

189
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:15,551
That's why I believe it's time to cut
all your relations with all the Ferells.

190
00:13:18,193 --> 00:13:21,270
I know it's difficult to believe...

191
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:24,301
but they are the only ones
who have a reason to do this.

192
00:13:26,073 --> 00:13:27,399
What's happening?

193
00:13:27,399 --> 00:13:29,270
I don't know with this guy.

194
00:13:32,295 --> 00:13:34,324
What are you doing?

195
00:13:46,049 --> 00:13:49,254
The target was either me
or your grandfather that night.

196
00:13:49,895 --> 00:13:53,048
It just so happened
that it was you and your mom who were in the car,

197
00:13:53,048 --> 00:13:54,762
and not me.

198
00:13:58,059 --> 00:14:00,458
Your mother protected you.

199
00:14:00,458 --> 00:14:04,379
And I believe she sacrificed her life
saving you.

200
00:14:07,723 --> 00:14:09,137
That's why...

201
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:15,629
I vow to do everything just to protect you.

202
00:14:18,056 --> 00:14:22,947
That's why I hope you'll understand
this favor I'm asking you, Celestina.

203
00:14:22,947 --> 00:14:27,085
Cut all your ties with the Ferells.

204
00:14:27,085 --> 00:14:30,421
They are a threat to our family.

205
00:14:30,421 --> 00:14:32,801
And most importantly...

206
00:14:33,524 --> 00:14:37,824
you must never forgive them
for what they did to Alyanna.

207
00:14:56,748 --> 00:15:00,485
<i>She was killed by the Ferells, Celestina.</i>

208
00:15:00,485 --> 00:15:03,721
<i>They killed your mother.</i>

209
00:15:03,721 --> 00:15:10,828
<i>That's why I believe it's time to cut
all your relations with all the Ferells.</i>

210
00:15:10,828 --> 00:15:13,264
Your mother protected you.

211
00:15:13,264 --> 00:15:17,187
And I believe she sacrificed her life
saving you.

212
00:15:20,428 --> 00:15:22,132
That's why...

213
00:15:22,774 --> 00:15:28,328
I vow to do everything just to protect you.

214
00:15:30,848 --> 00:15:35,720
That's why I hope you'll understand
this favor I'm asking you, Celestina.

215
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:39,824
Cut all your ties with the Ferells.

216
00:15:39,824 --> 00:15:43,261
They are a threat to our family.

217
00:15:43,261 --> 00:15:45,554
And most importantly...

218
00:15:46,197 --> 00:15:50,640
<i>you must never forgive them
for what they did to Alyanna.</i>

219
00:16:15,511 --> 00:16:17,435
Hello, Florence?

220
00:16:18,529 --> 00:16:20,398
Why?

221
00:16:20,398 --> 00:16:22,818
Do you miss me already?

222
00:16:24,001 --> 00:16:25,810
Nero...

223
00:16:25,810 --> 00:16:28,154
we need to talk.

224
00:16:32,505 --> 00:16:34,212
Oh, you're there.

225
00:16:34,212 --> 00:16:38,935
I'm always here, but you barely notice me.

226
00:16:39,884 --> 00:16:41,486
Wow.

227
00:16:41,486 --> 00:16:43,216
Here, ham?

228
00:16:44,337 --> 00:16:45,456
Hey, buddy.

229
00:16:45,456 --> 00:16:47,925
How was your sleep? Was it good?

230
00:16:47,925 --> 00:16:50,911
The truth is, I didn't sleep well last night.

231
00:16:51,638 --> 00:16:53,631
We're the same, Federico.

232
00:16:53,631 --> 00:16:55,466
I barely slept.

233
00:16:55,466 --> 00:17:00,138
I stayed up late watching
"Strangers in the Nights of Things".

234
00:17:00,138 --> 00:17:01,920
The twists are beautiful.

235
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:05,542
You thought all the characters
are nothing but...

236
00:17:05,542 --> 00:17:09,743
Iking, don't be a spoiler.

237
00:17:09,743 --> 00:17:13,551
And you even have an account,
but you refuse to share it.

238
00:17:13,551 --> 00:17:17,688
No, I just used the password
of my ex-girlfriend.

239
00:17:17,688 --> 00:17:19,056
She still hasn't changed it.

240
00:17:19,056 --> 00:17:21,959
May I borrow the password?

241
00:17:21,959 --> 00:17:23,275
Okay.

242
00:17:24,862 --> 00:17:28,099
Actually, the reason why
I wasn't able to sleep well last night

243
00:17:28,099 --> 00:17:31,335
is that I kept thinking
about what Don Ferell said.

244
00:17:31,335 --> 00:17:34,972
We should know who killed Alyanna.

245
00:17:34,972 --> 00:17:37,743
So we can be sure that Florence is safe.

246
00:17:43,859 --> 00:17:45,563
Anyway...

247
00:17:45,563 --> 00:17:50,055
don't you remember anything, buddy? Anything.

248
00:17:52,156 --> 00:17:55,459
Well, I didn't eat.

249
00:17:55,459 --> 00:17:56,761
What do you mean you didn't eat?

250
00:17:56,761 --> 00:18:00,131
I ordered three cups of rice,
but you took another one.

251
00:18:00,131 --> 00:18:01,966
If you think about it.

252
00:18:01,966 --> 00:18:04,569
Wait, I feel dizzy.

253
00:18:04,569 --> 00:18:07,405
Oh no, that's what I'm telling you.

254
00:18:07,405 --> 00:18:10,741
Okay later, let's drink medicine.

255
00:18:10,741 --> 00:18:11,943
What medicine?

256
00:18:11,943 --> 00:18:15,627
Well, I'll take care of it.

257
00:18:15,627 --> 00:18:19,173
Let's go. You're sleepy, and your head hurts.
Let's go home.

258
00:18:19,173 --> 00:18:20,518
- Come on.
- I feel dizzy.

259
00:18:20,518 --> 00:18:21,993
Okay, let's go.

260
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:28,847
Mister, have you seen a woman pass by here?

261
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:31,644
No.

262
00:18:32,689 --> 00:18:33,724
No?

263
00:18:33,724 --> 00:18:35,189
No.

264
00:18:35,889 --> 00:18:37,407
Okay, thank you.

265
00:18:40,152 --> 00:18:40,868
Just a little.

266
00:18:40,868 --> 00:18:45,439
Maybe I can remember
the shape of the head, the shape of his eyes.

267
00:18:47,663 --> 00:18:49,433
You know...

268
00:18:49,434 --> 00:18:51,733
why don't we ask someone to draw a sketch?

269
00:18:51,734 --> 00:18:54,500
If there's a suspect,
they make a drawing, right?

270
00:18:54,501 --> 00:18:56,207
Yes, that's right. There's a name for that.

271
00:18:56,207 --> 00:19:00,544
Cartographic sketch artist.

272
00:19:00,544 --> 00:19:02,613
Yes, that's the one.

273
00:19:02,613 --> 00:19:04,085
That's me.

274
00:19:05,282 --> 00:19:07,085
You haven't asked...

275
00:19:07,885 --> 00:19:10,023
Good thing you asked.

276
00:19:10,788 --> 00:19:15,186
Before I became a mailman,
I was a former cartographic sketch artist.

277
00:19:15,186 --> 00:19:18,629
That's the position I applied for
in the municipal's office.

278
00:19:18,629 --> 00:19:24,077
But the thing is, they made me a mailman.

279
00:19:25,196 --> 00:19:31,509
Wow.
From cartographic, to gardener, to mailman?

280
00:19:31,509 --> 00:19:33,471
I need to earn money.

281
00:19:33,471 --> 00:19:35,780
I need to find a side hustle.

282
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:38,410
Before, there was a movie,
and they made me an extra.

283
00:19:38,410 --> 00:19:40,084
And do you know what the role is?

284
00:19:40,084 --> 00:19:41,886
Boy-next-door.

285
00:19:41,886 --> 00:19:43,581
Dramatic actor.

286
00:19:43,581 --> 00:19:45,353
I can do everything.

287
00:19:45,353 --> 00:19:51,162
I need to save,
so you know, I can settle down with my girl.

288
00:19:51,162 --> 00:19:52,410
Really?

289
00:19:52,410 --> 00:19:54,058
Do you have a girl?

290
00:19:54,058 --> 00:19:59,537
Well, do you think you're the only one
who has Babycakes in this story?

291
00:19:59,537 --> 00:20:01,238
Wait, wait. We might go off-topic.

292
00:20:01,238 --> 00:20:03,274
Is it true that you can draw?

293
00:20:03,274 --> 00:20:06,030
Yes. That's true.

294
00:20:19,657 --> 00:20:22,560
Just tell me, and I'll take care of it.

295
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,537
Let me know what he looks like.

296
00:20:35,973 --> 00:20:38,709
I'm sorry, Ms. Florence Almero,

297
00:20:38,709 --> 00:20:41,648
but they cannot go inside the school.

298
00:20:41,648 --> 00:20:46,144
After the incident that happened last time,

299
00:20:46,144 --> 00:20:51,689
I cannot risk another commotion happening
inside the school premises.

300
00:20:51,689 --> 00:20:55,926
I'm sorry, Ms. Almero,
but I have made my final decision.

301
00:20:55,926 --> 00:21:00,965
I cannot and I will not allow
your security people

302
00:21:00,965 --> 00:21:03,882
to get inside the premises of this building.

303
00:21:08,001 --> 00:21:10,733
Just wait for me outside.

304
00:21:10,734 --> 00:21:13,167
But Ms. Florence,
your grandfather instructed us...

305
00:21:13,167 --> 00:21:14,833
To keep me safe.

306
00:21:14,834 --> 00:21:15,871
- Yes.
- That's right.

307
00:21:15,871 --> 00:21:16,945
Yes.

308
00:21:18,949 --> 00:21:20,317
Don't worry,

309
00:21:20,317 --> 00:21:24,155
I think nothing bad will happen to me
inside the school.

310
00:21:24,155 --> 00:21:27,090
And Dean is right.

311
00:21:27,090 --> 00:21:33,166
We attracted conflict on the first day
that compromised the security,

312
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:34,638
and that's you.

313
00:21:35,939 --> 00:21:39,833
But if I need you,
I will call you as soon as possible.

314
00:21:39,834 --> 00:21:41,548
Okay.

315
00:21:41,548 --> 00:21:42,770
Let's go.

316
00:21:47,278 --> 00:21:50,881
Thank you, Ms. Florence.
You handled that really well.

317
00:21:50,881 --> 00:21:54,351
You are truly one of our brightest students.

318
00:21:54,351 --> 00:21:57,087
You're welcome, Dean.

319
00:21:57,087 --> 00:21:58,889
By the way, come with me.

320
00:21:58,889 --> 00:22:01,315
There's something we need to talk about.

321
00:22:09,667 --> 00:22:14,805
Dean Alvaro, my grades are okay.
They're all good, right?

322
00:22:14,805 --> 00:22:17,392
Why do you need to talk to me?

323
00:22:18,782 --> 00:22:20,905
Am I in trouble?

324
00:22:20,905 --> 00:22:25,149
Will I be suspended
because of what my bodyguards did?

325
00:22:25,149 --> 00:22:27,404
The truth is, I don't want that,

326
00:22:27,404 --> 00:22:30,421
but there's nothing I can do,
because that's what my daddy wants.

327
00:22:30,421 --> 00:22:32,156
Just follow me.

328
00:22:32,156 --> 00:22:36,093
But why do you have to talk to me
when I didn't do anything?

329
00:22:36,093 --> 00:22:40,859
It's because there's someone
who wants to talk to you, Florence.

330
00:22:50,908 --> 00:22:52,578
I spoke to Nero last night,

331
00:22:52,578 --> 00:22:55,558
and he was telling me about your concerns.

332
00:23:00,184 --> 00:23:06,590
Is it true that you have something to do
with what happened to my mommy?

333
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:08,510
Lorenzo was right.

334
00:23:09,487 --> 00:23:14,795
Our business rivalry became intense.

335
00:23:14,795 --> 00:23:18,574
I was so mad, I was able to say bad words

336
00:23:18,574 --> 00:23:21,459
to Rogelio, in front of Lorenzo.

337
00:23:23,274 --> 00:23:27,249
I was fuming mad, but I was in pain.

338
00:23:28,212 --> 00:23:31,319
I was angry at the prospect
of losing my wife.

339
00:23:31,319 --> 00:23:36,694
I vented out my anger
towards the business ventures with Rogelio,

340
00:23:36,694 --> 00:23:42,722
that's why I said bad and hurtful words
in front of Lorenzo.

341
00:23:44,842 --> 00:23:51,215
But your Grandma Amanda made me realize
not to get mad

342
00:23:51,215 --> 00:23:54,503
and accept the time that we have.

343
00:23:56,053 --> 00:23:58,422
She lived for years.

344
00:23:58,422 --> 00:24:03,971
But she saw and got to know
her five grandchildren.

345
00:24:07,264 --> 00:24:10,534
It was a struggle...

346
00:24:10,534 --> 00:24:13,760
and every moment of it was special.

347
00:24:15,606 --> 00:24:17,374
I have many sins, Florence,

348
00:24:17,374 --> 00:24:21,135
but I can never do
what Lorenzo is accusing me of.

349
00:24:22,393 --> 00:24:27,584
I can't deprive you of your right
to know your own mother...

350
00:24:27,584 --> 00:24:30,736
and have a complete family.

351
00:25:03,300 --> 00:25:07,090
Florence, sorry, but there's trouble again.

352
00:25:07,090 --> 00:25:09,026
What do you mean there's trouble?

353
00:25:09,026 --> 00:25:13,997
It's your bodyguards and the Ferells.
They're fighting again.

354
00:25:13,997 --> 00:25:16,627
- Where?
- Over there.

355
00:25:24,976 --> 00:25:27,018
These heels are such a problem.

356
00:25:27,711 --> 00:25:32,666
Hey Ferell guys, what did you do again?
This spells trouble again.

357
00:25:33,951 --> 00:25:35,948
What's so funny?

358
00:25:38,455 --> 00:25:40,174
What?

359
00:25:45,863 --> 00:25:49,901
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

360
00:25:53,804 --> 00:25:57,307
Group hug!

361
00:25:57,307 --> 00:25:59,495
Group hug!

362
00:26:03,113 --> 00:26:04,893
Turn around.

363
00:26:08,218 --> 00:26:10,870
- Let's go!
- Yes.

364
00:26:11,989 --> 00:26:15,626
Okay guys, let's set some ground rules.

365
00:26:15,626 --> 00:26:18,595
No more talking about Florence
being an Almero.

366
00:26:18,595 --> 00:26:20,520
Okay, that's enough.

367
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:25,096
In this space, she is just Florence.

368
00:26:26,503 --> 00:26:29,506
Besides, there are a lot of things
we need to talk about,

369
00:26:29,506 --> 00:26:31,422
like, how is she and Nero.

370
00:26:31,422 --> 00:26:35,557
And what's the stage of their relationship.

371
00:26:35,557 --> 00:26:37,180
There you go.

372
00:26:37,180 --> 00:26:40,517
And you're asking me those questions, Lina?

373
00:26:40,517 --> 00:26:45,714
Shouldn't we be talking
about you and Troy now?

374
00:26:47,738 --> 00:26:50,093
What? Hot seat.

375
00:26:50,093 --> 00:26:51,531
What?

376
00:26:51,531 --> 00:26:53,764
We just followed your advice, Florence.

377
00:26:53,764 --> 00:26:57,133
We're not yet there, but it's getting there.

378
00:26:57,133 --> 00:26:58,534
Wow...

379
00:26:58,534 --> 00:27:01,605
So now it's my fault?

380
00:27:01,605 --> 00:27:04,076
I already helped.

381
00:27:04,942 --> 00:27:07,811
Wow, that's so thrilling.

382
00:27:07,811 --> 00:27:12,282
Well as for me and Tristan,
we're getting there too.

383
00:27:12,282 --> 00:27:14,284
Hey, stop it.

384
00:27:14,284 --> 00:27:17,328
The last thing I want in this world
is to be your trophy boyfriend.

385
00:27:17,328 --> 00:27:19,923
Hey, you're too harsh.

386
00:27:19,923 --> 00:27:22,593
But that's impressive,

387
00:27:22,593 --> 00:27:29,766
because Tristan prefers a more profound
and meaningful relationship.

388
00:27:29,766 --> 00:27:32,536
- That's my bet.
- Trophy husband?

389
00:27:32,536 --> 00:27:34,764
It's possible!

390
00:27:35,505 --> 00:27:37,264
It's really possible.

391
00:27:38,175 --> 00:27:41,378
Oh, by the way guys...

392
00:27:41,378 --> 00:27:45,082
Let's make Aldus and Aira our role models.

393
00:27:45,082 --> 00:27:47,017
They're just chill.

394
00:27:47,017 --> 00:27:49,820
What do you mean just chill?

395
00:27:49,820 --> 00:27:54,024
Aldus decided that we should stay friends.

396
00:27:54,024 --> 00:27:57,942
Aira, you're nice, I already told you that.

397
00:27:57,942 --> 00:28:00,945
But believe it or not,

398
00:28:00,945 --> 00:28:04,726
I'm not thinking about relationships
like that yet.

399
00:28:04,726 --> 00:28:06,384
That's because you're just a playboy.

400
00:28:06,384 --> 00:28:09,339
Sounds like an excuse just to say no to Aira.

401
00:28:09,339 --> 00:28:11,608
Of course not, Antonia.

402
00:28:11,608 --> 00:28:13,877
Aira is an amazing person,

403
00:28:13,877 --> 00:28:17,900
but I hope one day our paths will cross,

404
00:28:17,901 --> 00:28:21,585
and when we see each other again,

405
00:28:21,585 --> 00:28:22,967
we both want the same things in life.

406
00:28:22,968 --> 00:28:23,854
Wow.

407
00:28:23,854 --> 00:28:25,489
Well, you're just a playboy.

408
00:28:25,489 --> 00:28:29,459
If our paths really do cross, Aldus,

409
00:28:29,459 --> 00:28:31,128
probably I'm taken already.

410
00:28:31,128 --> 00:28:32,596
By Aldus Ferell?

411
00:28:32,596 --> 00:28:35,298
Possibly, dating Tom Holland.

412
00:28:35,298 --> 00:28:38,735
- You're something else.
- What a pity for Zendaya.

413
00:28:38,735 --> 00:28:41,170
- Yes.
- Don't you like Gagamboy?

414
00:28:44,541 --> 00:28:45,842
How about you, Owen?

415
00:28:45,842 --> 00:28:49,079
Well actually, I'm with Aldus on this one.

416
00:28:49,079 --> 00:28:51,913
Dating isn't really my priority right now.

417
00:28:53,784 --> 00:28:56,086
- I want to travel.
- With Antonia.

418
00:28:56,086 --> 00:28:57,821
- Explore the world.
- With Antonia.

419
00:28:57,821 --> 00:28:59,556
- By myself.
- With Antonia.

420
00:28:59,556 --> 00:29:01,591
- By myself.
- With Antonia.

421
00:29:01,591 --> 00:29:03,222
She's your world.

422
00:29:05,862 --> 00:29:08,132
Hey, that's cool.

423
00:29:09,205 --> 00:29:12,469
No, but that really just sounds
like a fun idea.

424
00:29:12,469 --> 00:29:15,807
How about you, Florence? Do you have plans?

425
00:29:21,411 --> 00:29:23,349
Do you have any plans?

426
00:29:37,608 --> 00:29:38,995
Come on, take that bite.

427
00:29:38,995 --> 00:29:42,090
- Yes!
- Yes!

428
00:29:42,090 --> 00:29:46,203
Oh, let's take a selfie for this cute moment.
Right, guys?

429
00:29:46,203 --> 00:29:47,971
- Let's remember this.
- Troy?

430
00:29:47,971 --> 00:29:50,240
Take a photo for us.

431
00:29:50,240 --> 00:29:52,035
- Let's do a selfie.
- Selfie!

432
00:29:52,035 --> 00:29:53,610
So, you want a selfie,
but you want me to take a picture?

433
00:29:53,610 --> 00:29:55,471
Yes.

434
00:29:58,915 --> 00:30:01,479
- One, two, three.
- Take one without you.

435
00:30:03,553 --> 00:30:05,464
One, two, three.

436
00:30:07,858 --> 00:30:10,784
- Wacky!
- Wacky!

437
00:30:17,701 --> 00:30:19,387
Well, it's like...

438
00:30:21,371 --> 00:30:24,935
Maybe the same as my head,
but a little more...

439
00:30:26,107 --> 00:30:30,929
Maybe the cheeks are chubby.

440
00:30:30,929 --> 00:30:33,443
Wait, chubby cheeks?

441
00:30:34,433 --> 00:30:35,786
James?

442
00:30:36,466 --> 00:30:38,624
And you have all the food.

443
00:30:38,624 --> 00:30:40,374
How can we eat breakfast?

444
00:30:40,374 --> 00:30:42,605
- Go ahead and get some.
- Huh?

445
00:30:42,605 --> 00:30:44,452
You're something else.

446
00:30:44,452 --> 00:30:46,913
That's why you're not being noticed.

447
00:30:46,913 --> 00:30:48,974
And, then?

448
00:30:50,607 --> 00:30:54,818
And I'm sure his eyes are scary.

449
00:30:54,818 --> 00:30:57,294
It's like he won't do anything nice.

450
00:31:00,417 --> 00:31:01,518
What?

451
00:31:01,518 --> 00:31:03,240
Did you get it?

452
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:06,397
You know what, Federico?

453
00:31:06,397 --> 00:31:10,458
I think I know the person you're describing.

454
00:31:10,458 --> 00:31:14,529
It looks like he won't do anything good.

455
00:31:17,134 --> 00:31:18,873
Is this the one?

456
00:31:23,986 --> 00:31:28,716
You know, you're full of nonsense.

457
00:31:31,114 --> 00:31:32,516
But in fairness,

458
00:31:32,516 --> 00:31:36,138
the way he looks, he won't do anything good.

459
00:31:37,255 --> 00:31:40,524
Well, I tried to draw it

460
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:46,930
based on what you're saying,
but it's really vague.

461
00:31:46,930 --> 00:31:50,233
It's worse than my love life.

462
00:31:50,233 --> 00:31:51,935
And you even blame others.

463
00:31:51,935 --> 00:31:54,204
You know, Federico, let's just be patient.

464
00:31:54,204 --> 00:31:58,167
You'll eventually remember his face,
and how he looks like.

465
00:31:59,843 --> 00:32:01,812
My grandfather once said...

466
00:32:01,812 --> 00:32:07,120
Why is your grandfather included here?

467
00:32:08,785 --> 00:32:11,455
My grandfather once said...

468
00:32:11,455 --> 00:32:16,467
that if you return
to the scene of the crime...

469
00:32:16,467 --> 00:32:23,400
it might trigger
and make you remember what happened.

470
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:27,838
In fairness to your grandfather,
he has a point.

471
00:32:27,838 --> 00:32:29,198
Federico...

472
00:32:29,973 --> 00:32:33,877
Why don't go back to the scene of the crime?

473
00:32:33,877 --> 00:32:35,145
You're right.

474
00:32:35,145 --> 00:32:36,780
That's a good suggestion.

475
00:32:36,780 --> 00:32:38,081
Let's do that.

476
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:40,784
Yes.

477
00:32:48,391 --> 00:32:50,923
Why didn't you answer Antonia?

478
00:32:52,338 --> 00:32:54,364
That's because...

479
00:32:54,364 --> 00:32:57,300
I don't know what to answer.

480
00:32:57,300 --> 00:33:03,142
It seems for the first time in my life,
I have no plans.

481
00:33:04,950 --> 00:33:09,345
Imagine, my dream before...

482
00:33:10,456 --> 00:33:13,784
was just to finish my studies on time.

483
00:33:13,784 --> 00:33:17,821
And support my parents...

484
00:33:17,821 --> 00:33:22,726
and bring them to Europe and Boracay.

485
00:33:22,726 --> 00:33:25,749
These are the dreams of a simple person.

486
00:33:26,505 --> 00:33:33,061
Well, with my situation right now,
it's difficult to dream.

487
00:33:34,571 --> 00:33:40,772
How can you dream
if you have an influential family?

488
00:33:43,446 --> 00:33:46,229
How does an Almero dream?

489
00:33:50,287 --> 00:33:52,713
The truth is...

490
00:33:52,713 --> 00:33:56,174
even I have no idea what to do tomorrow.

491
00:33:57,418 --> 00:34:00,221
But I only know one thing for sure.

492
00:34:00,973 --> 00:34:04,010
Whatever is waiting for me in the future...

493
00:34:04,734 --> 00:34:07,065
I want to be with you.

494
00:34:09,940 --> 00:34:12,142
Wow.

495
00:34:12,142 --> 00:34:15,213
My heart has really fallen for you.

496
00:34:16,285 --> 00:34:19,799
I don't know
what kind of future is waiting for us.

497
00:34:20,602 --> 00:34:22,588
But what I only know is...

498
00:34:23,687 --> 00:34:28,198
I love you so much.

499
00:34:29,674 --> 00:34:41,049
And I love you so much too,
Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell.

500
00:35:11,401 --> 00:35:13,982
What's this about, Garpidio?

501
00:35:13,982 --> 00:35:16,036
You know what this is all about.

502
00:35:16,036 --> 00:35:18,208
This is about Florence.

503
00:35:19,109 --> 00:35:20,872
She is my granddaughter...

504
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:24,349
and you don't have anything
to do with her life.

505
00:35:25,245 --> 00:35:28,351
That's where you're wrong, Rogelio.

506
00:35:28,351 --> 00:35:32,522
Florence has been with us,
and she's been a part of our family.

507
00:35:32,522 --> 00:35:35,325
Come on, Garpidio.

508
00:35:35,325 --> 00:35:38,495
Do you really want
to get everything that I have?

509
00:35:38,495 --> 00:35:40,263
I didn't get anything from you, Rogelio.

510
00:35:40,263 --> 00:35:41,947
Enough already.

511
00:35:43,300 --> 00:35:45,533
I look up to you like a big brother.

512
00:35:46,169 --> 00:35:48,775
I treated you like a real brother.

513
00:35:49,456 --> 00:35:51,290
And what did you do to me?

514
00:35:52,175 --> 00:35:54,844
You took Amanda away from me...

515
00:35:54,844 --> 00:35:57,025
even if you knew that I love her so much.

516
00:35:57,853 --> 00:35:58,823
And now here you are,

517
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:03,818
trying to take her, Florence,
away from me and my son.

518
00:36:05,498 --> 00:36:09,732
I'm sorry
if you thought I took Amanda away from you.

519
00:36:10,593 --> 00:36:12,762
Sorry... That's what you're good at.
Saying sorry.

520
00:36:12,762 --> 00:36:17,232
Maybe you should also be sorry
for Alyanna's death.

521
00:36:17,232 --> 00:36:20,503
Do you really believe
I am capable of killing Alyanna?

522
00:36:20,503 --> 00:36:22,539
I was your target that night.

523
00:36:22,539 --> 00:36:24,732
You ordered to have me killed.

524
00:36:26,201 --> 00:36:28,979
- Why would I do that?
- I don't know!

525
00:36:28,979 --> 00:36:31,614
Maybe because
I'm getting ahead of you in business.

526
00:36:31,614 --> 00:36:33,817
Or maybe you're getting satisfaction

527
00:36:33,817 --> 00:36:36,953
whenever you see your rivals suffering.

528
00:36:36,953 --> 00:36:39,930
Please, Garpidio...

529
00:36:39,930 --> 00:36:44,627
You and your grandsons
should leave Florence alone.

530
00:36:44,627 --> 00:36:48,459
We will never have a Ferell
become part of our family.

531
00:36:49,499 --> 00:36:51,134
Never.

532
00:36:51,134 --> 00:36:52,478
You're right.

533
00:36:52,478 --> 00:36:54,318
I wanted to see you suffer.

534
00:36:55,071 --> 00:36:59,396
I got mad at you
for not understanding that Amanda loved me.

535
00:37:01,453 --> 00:37:02,200
I was disappointed

536
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:07,166
because I wanted to share that love
with my brother, my best friend.

537
00:37:07,167 --> 00:37:08,533
But what did you do?

538
00:37:08,534 --> 00:37:13,399
You looked at me as if I'm so evil.

539
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:15,625
When all I wanted to do was...

540
00:37:15,625 --> 00:37:19,987
to love the person who loves me.

541
00:37:21,097 --> 00:37:22,878
But I was wrong.

542
00:37:24,234 --> 00:37:29,134
Instead of understanding
the pain you're feeling...

543
00:37:31,875 --> 00:37:33,938
I was wrong to resent you.

544
00:37:36,615 --> 00:37:38,837
If I can only bring back time...

545
00:37:40,281 --> 00:37:43,829
I should've been a better friend to you.

546
00:37:45,493 --> 00:37:49,426
That's why I won't get tired
of asking for your forgiveness.

547
00:37:49,426 --> 00:37:50,693
I'm sorry.

548
00:37:50,693 --> 00:37:52,415
Sorry for everything.

549
00:37:56,540 --> 00:38:00,277
And because of that, I'm begging you.

550
00:38:00,277 --> 00:38:03,440
All our pain and hard feelings...

551
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:09,313
let's not pass them on to the kids.

552
00:38:27,768 --> 00:38:29,485
Why are you home late?

553
00:38:39,642 --> 00:38:42,045
I just did something in school.

554
00:38:42,045 --> 00:38:45,187
There are people I needed to talk to.

555
00:38:48,718 --> 00:38:50,648
Do you think I'm stupid?

556
00:38:51,621 --> 00:38:54,992
Do you think I'm here to play dumb?

557
00:38:55,865 --> 00:38:58,228
I was with George earlier.

558
00:38:58,228 --> 00:38:59,773
Remember him?

559
00:39:00,806 --> 00:39:02,586
Camille's father.

560
00:39:04,075 --> 00:39:06,868
He told me
about what happened between you and Camille.

561
00:39:06,868 --> 00:39:08,399
The incident...

562
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:09,700
And it made him realize

563
00:39:09,701 --> 00:39:13,366
that he needs to fix his relationship
with his daughter.

564
00:39:13,367 --> 00:39:18,648
He told me you were instrumental
in making him realize that.

565
00:39:18,648 --> 00:39:21,007
And I was so proud of you...

566
00:39:22,125 --> 00:39:24,523
until he showed me this.

567
00:39:33,763 --> 00:39:36,766
It looks like
you haven't informed your friends

568
00:39:36,766 --> 00:39:41,359
not to post pictures with the Ferells.

569
00:39:47,159 --> 00:39:48,845
Please let me explain.

570
00:39:48,845 --> 00:39:50,327
Explain?

571
00:39:51,428 --> 00:39:53,082
What else do we need to talk about?

572
00:39:53,082 --> 00:39:55,597
We already have an agreement.

573
00:39:58,106 --> 00:40:01,534
I already told you to avoid the Ferells.

574
00:40:05,768 --> 00:40:08,090
I'm sorry, but...

575
00:40:08,698 --> 00:40:11,229
I can't do what you want.

576
00:40:13,970 --> 00:40:16,726
Because the Ferells are my friends.

577
00:40:17,714 --> 00:40:22,766
Tristan, Aldus, Troy, and Owen
are my friends.

578
00:40:23,646 --> 00:40:28,318
Grandpa Garp is close to my heart.

579
00:40:28,318 --> 00:40:33,423
And most importantly, I love Nero.

580
00:40:33,423 --> 00:40:38,020
You would rather choose those killers
than your own mother?

581
00:40:41,272 --> 00:40:43,700
I don't believe in that.

582
00:40:43,700 --> 00:40:47,912
Because I know Grandpa Garp is not capable
of what you're accusing him of.

583
00:40:49,076 --> 00:40:51,143
Can you hear yourself?

584
00:40:51,941 --> 00:40:54,043
They brainwashed you.

585
00:40:54,043 --> 00:40:57,244
They made you believe their lies.

586
00:40:58,781 --> 00:41:00,986
I am not dumb.

587
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:04,320
I have a mind of my own.

588
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:06,823
I also have my own understanding.

589
00:41:06,823 --> 00:41:11,094
And if there's a victim here, that's you.

590
00:41:11,094 --> 00:41:14,471
You're a victim of your own anger.

591
00:41:14,471 --> 00:41:18,044
You're a victim of the pain you felt
when you lost Mommy.

592
00:41:18,044 --> 00:41:19,102
Why?

593
00:41:19,102 --> 00:41:21,371
Because you weren't able to protect her.

594
00:41:21,371 --> 00:41:23,506
You failed to save her.

595
00:41:23,506 --> 00:41:25,708
That's why you're looking
for someone else to blame

596
00:41:25,708 --> 00:41:28,344
because of your own failure.

597
00:41:28,344 --> 00:41:31,441
Because you knew deep in you
that you once neglected your family.

598
00:41:31,441 --> 00:41:33,416
That's why you lost me, right?

599
00:41:33,416 --> 00:41:34,719
Enough!

600
00:41:36,291 --> 00:41:38,206
Go to your room!

601
00:41:38,206 --> 00:41:39,505
Pack your bags.

602
00:41:39,505 --> 00:41:43,248
I'm pulling you out of the university
and taking you with me to the States.

603
00:42:02,545 --> 00:42:05,782
Are you sure where we're going?

604
00:42:05,782 --> 00:42:07,950
We're getting lost already.

605
00:42:07,950 --> 00:42:09,152
Don't pressure me.

606
00:42:09,152 --> 00:42:11,341
That was 17 years ago.

607
00:42:12,017 --> 00:42:13,265
Wait.

608
00:42:14,257 --> 00:42:15,493
I remember something.

609
00:42:15,493 --> 00:42:17,593
There. Wait, hold on.

610
00:42:17,593 --> 00:42:18,661
- Okay, go.
- Yes, that's right.

611
00:42:18,661 --> 00:42:19,529
Okay, okay.

612
00:42:19,529 --> 00:42:21,030
Okay.

613
00:42:21,030 --> 00:42:22,804
I don't need your help...

614
00:42:24,634 --> 00:42:27,270
Unless you'll help me get inside
the mansion of the Almeros

615
00:42:27,270 --> 00:42:29,366
to get Florence.

616
00:42:29,367 --> 00:42:30,633
And then what?

617
00:42:30,634 --> 00:42:33,743
You'll elope and live happily ever after?

618
00:42:33,743 --> 00:42:37,343
Maybe that's another cartoon character.

619
00:42:37,954 --> 00:42:40,347
No. This time, it's for real.

620
00:42:40,347 --> 00:42:43,784
- Look, this is a real person.
- Let me see.

621
00:42:43,784 --> 00:42:45,290
Federico, look at this.

622
00:42:46,622 --> 00:42:48,558
This is the one.

623
00:42:48,558 --> 00:42:49,525
Who is that?

624
00:42:49,525 --> 00:42:50,693
Celestina!

625
00:42:50,693 --> 00:42:51,794
Dad!

626
00:42:51,794 --> 00:42:54,197
Where is she? Celestina is missing.

627
00:42:54,197 --> 00:42:56,799
Lorenzo, it is your fault...

628
00:42:56,799 --> 00:42:59,431
why Florence rebelled.

629
00:42:59,431 --> 00:43:00,901
Florence?

630
00:43:02,405 --> 00:43:03,406
What's happening?

631
00:43:03,406 --> 00:43:05,468
I saw Florence.

632
00:43:06,409 --> 00:43:08,177
Maybe your eyes are
just playing tricks on you.

633
00:43:08,177 --> 00:43:11,086
I can't make a mistake.
I really saw her face.

634
00:43:12,674 --> 00:43:14,066
Nero?
